From fd3f5e35af8e3e2d21c8169ec00e76c9aeb13efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tesseract XRT port <jwkim@limagin.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:15:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] xocl: constify sysfs bin_attribute callbacks and lists
 (Linux 6.16)

Two mainline v6.16 changes break every binary sysfs attribute in the
tree (icap, mailbox, xmc, xmc_u2, xgq_vmr, ert, ...):
 - commit 97d06802d10a ("sysfs: constify bin_attribute argument of
   bin_attribute::read/write()") makes the callbacks take
   "const struct bin_attribute *";
 - commit 9bec944506fa ("sysfs: constify attribute_group::bin_attrs")
   makes the group member "const struct bin_attribute *const *", and a
   "struct bin_attribute **" no longer converts to it in C.

xocl_drv.h gains BIN_ATTRIBUTE_CONST (the name XRT upstream uses), and
it is applied to the attr parameter of the 42 read/write callbacks
(including the QSFP ones generated by macros in xmc.c / xmc_u2.c) and
to the element type of the 15 *_bin_attrs[] arrays. The bin_attribute
objects themselves stay writable.

Guard: LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(6, 16, 0). Mainline v6.13 ..
v6.15 carry the transitional read_new/write_new/bin_attrs_new members
while read/write/bin_attrs are still non-const, so the old declarations
remain correct there; v6.16, 6.17.0-35 and 7.0.0-x have only the const
forms. Before 6.16 the macro is empty and the code is unchanged.

Equivalence: qualifier-only change. None of the callbacks writes
through attr (it would no longer compile), so the generated code is the
same.

Upstream: XRT commit f41db917c introduces the same macro and guard; it
additionally makes some bin_attribute objects const, which is not
required and is left out here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SpY5QiU1d7kAe8YJM35EvA
